rl":"https://github.com/TuguiDragos/Peel/releases/download/v1.1.0/Peel-1.1.0.zip"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TuguiDragos/Peel/tarball/v1.1.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TuguiDragos/Peel/zipball/v1.1.0","body":"Peel 1.1.0 updates itself from now on, sets apart what only an administrator can remove, and protects more of what nothing could bring back.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Peel 1.0.1 can't update itself. Quit it, move it from Applications to the Trash, and drag the new Peel into Applications: your History, exclusions, and settings stay. If Homebrew installed it, run `brew upgrade --cask peel` instead. If Home then says the helper isn't answering, choose Repair.\n\n## Install\n\n- **Download** `Peel-1.1.0.dmg` below and drag Peel into Applications. It's signed by its developer and notarized by Apple.\n- **Homebrew:** `brew install --cask tuguidragos/tap/peel`\n\nRequires macOS Tahoe 26 or later.\n\n## Highlights\n\n- **Updates itself**, when you choose and once it has checked that the update is signed as Peel's.\n- **Needs an Administrator:** Orphaned Files lists apart what only an administrator can remove, and says how.\n- **Safer:** never moves what syncs to your other devices, holds back what may exist only on your Mac, and knows more browser wallets.\n- **More to clean:** the models more AI apps download, 45 more build tools, and more developer caches.\n- **Every translation** read again, in macOS's own words.\n\n[Everything that changed in 1.1.0](https://github.com/TuguiDragos/Peel/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md#110-2026-10-14)\n\n## Checksums\n\n| File | SHA-256 |\n|---|---|\n| `Peel-1.1.0.dmg` | `c1add2aac4cb8cbb30a5187787bda31656da808caf4f2d1f51a7b175773d0a34` |\n| `Peel-1.1.0.zip` | `37fb0dcc483039aefc2652e16f8e2a1dc86a7da2f24bfa482c872c8661939e92` |\n\nFound a problem? [Open an issue](https://github.com/TuguiDragos/Peel/issues/new/choose), or report a security problem privately, as [SECURITY.md](https://github.com/TuguiDragos/Peel/blob/main/SECURITY.md) describes.\n"}